  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.713 accuracy at 6.22 GPU hours. With only one data point, the key uncertainty is whether the expensive transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler avgpool aggregation captures most of the multiprofile benefit. This experiment (config_048) is a direct ablation: identical to config_004 except aggregation changes from transformer to avgpool, keeping weighted fusion. It will clarify whether the ~3+ GPU-hour overhead of transformer aggregation translates into meaningful accuracy gains. If avgpool matches or nearly matches 0.713, we save substantial GPU budget across the remaining 8 experiments for exploring other dimensions (image encoder, RNA encoder, fusion). If it drops notably, we confirm transformer is essential and can focus future budget on other levers. Expected relative cost: moderate (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), roughly half of config_004, since avgpool replaces the multi-head attention transformer while retaining multimodal + multiprofile processing."
}

